body:
I'm not fond of binding methods publicly as a private API.

It seems here it's only used in Viewport. Instead of doing:
```cpp
StringName set_text_method = SNAME("_set_text");
	if (!gui.key_focus || !gui.key_focus->has_method(set_text_method)) {
		return;
	}
	gui.key_focus->call(set_text_method, p_text, p_emit_signal);
```
You can simply cast the object to `LineEdit` and `TextEdit` successively to a public `set_text_no_signal`.

```cpp
LineEdit *line_edit = Object::cast_to<LineEdit>(gui.key_focus);
if (line_edit) {
    line_edit->set_text_no_signal(p_text);
}
TextEdit *text_edit = Object::cast_to<TextEdit>(gui.key_focus);
if (text_edit) {
    text_edit->set_text_no_signal(p_text);
}
```

Unless I'm missing something obviously.

